members.statement_original:
Let $\overline{Y}_{k}^{P}(B;\mathcal{D})$ denote the empirical mean of the reward of arm $k$ over bin $B$ in dataset $\mathcal{D}$, namely 
\[
\overline{Y}_{k}^{P}(B;\mathcal{D})\coloneqq
\begin{cases}
    \frac{1}{n_{k}^{P}(B;\mathcal{D})}\sum\limits_{(X_{i},\pi_{i},Y_{i})\in\mathcal{D}}Y \mathbb{1}\{X_{i}\in B,\,\pi_{i}=k\}, & \text{if }  n_{k}^{P}(B;\mathcal{D}) \neq 0, \\
    0, & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}\tag{8}
\]

algorithm_steps_original.text_original:
Define the reward function estimator $\widehat{f}_{k}(x;2^{-l_{i}}) \coloneqq\widehat{\eta}_{k}\big(x;B_{i}(x)\big)$, where 
\[
\widehat{\eta}_{k}(x;B) \coloneqq\frac{\sum_{(X_{t},Y_{t})\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathsf{se}}^{(k)}}Y_{t}\mathbb{1}\{X_{t}\in B\}}
{1 \vee \sum_{(X_{t},Y_{t})\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathsf{se}}^{(k)}}\mathbb{1}\{X_{t}\in B\}},\quad \forall B\in\mathcal{B}_{l_{i}}. 
\tag{16}
\]

algorithm_steps_original.source_tex:
